RESULT: 19/19 checks passed.
VERDICT (pre-tests): the ray kinematics of the pinned family is fixed by the null locus and two symmetry pairings.
  Redshift ratio cosh l_2/cosh l_1, weak-field coefficient 1/2; both local seat-to-seat transport rules FAIL (PT-1i/j);
  the null-structure horizon is the pinning's horizon; the orbit closes as an identity and, under KIN-2a, its
  deflection is 2 r_s/b + (15 pi/16)(r_s/b)^2 + ...  Conditional on KIN-2a, STAT-1, ROT-1, PROP-1.
COMPARISON STAGE: STAT-1/ROT-1 are the Killing-vector conservation laws of a stationary, spherically symmetric field;
  PROP-1 is the Painleve-Gullstrand / river picture (flat slice, inflow at the escape speed); PT-3d is Schwarzschild's
  null-geodesic equation; 2 r_s/b is Einstein 1915 (4GM/c^2 b), 15 pi/16 (r_s/b)^2 = (15 pi/4)(GM/c^2 b)^2 is the
  second-order light deflection (Epstein-Shapiro 1980); the weak-field 1/2 is Pound-Rebka.  The office ghost of PT-1i
  is the classical error of treating free-fall frames at different points as boosted copies of each other.
